{"study_accession":"PRJNA645689","secondary_study_accession":"SRP271450","title":"Newly defined Human Hematopoietic Stem Cell Populations","description":"Purpose: to compare the transcriptomic profile of the two most primitive human EPCR+ stem and CD90+EPCR- progenitor populations. Methods: cells were obtained from human cord-blood and flow-sorted using the surface antigens described. 5 EPCR+ and 4 CD90+EPCR- biological replicates were used to extract total RNA and quality was verified (RIN >8). Libraries were prepared using with 20-25 ng/sample of starting RNA. All samples were sequenced two independent times. Conclusions: this study represents the first analysis of transcriptomes from the two most primitive human stem/progenitor populations, with biologic replicates, generated by RNA-seq technology. The optimized data analysis workflows reported here should provide a framework for comparative investigations of expression profiles of other human blood stem/progenitor populations. Overall design: Transcriptomic profiling (RNA-seq) of the two most primitive human stem (CD34+CD38-CD45RA-EPCR+; hereafter EPCR+) and progenitor (CD34+CD38-CD45RA-CD90+EPCR-; hereafter CD90+EPCR-) populations.","pubmed":"35440586","geo_series":"","n_samples":9,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN15512857","study_accession":"PRJNA645689","blood_class":"cord_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"CD90+EPCR- HSC 9 [AFO296A39]","description":"CD90+EPCR- HSC 9 [AFO296A39]","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM4668033","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":2,"first_public":"2021-07-04","attributes":[["source_name","CD90+EPCR- HSC"],["age","post-natal"],["tissue","cord blood"],["cell_type","progenitor (CD34+CD38-CD45RA-CD90+EPCR-) cells"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR12203025","experiment_accession":"SRX8713872","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":11809060,"base_count":1192715060,"first_public":"2021-07-04","experiment_title":"Illumina HiS